<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Princess Alice of the United Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1843–1878</span> · Also known as Alice, Grand Duchess of Hesse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Princess Alice was the third child of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> and Prince Albert. In 1862 she married Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, who became Grand Duke Louis IV in 1877, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> she promoted nursing and women's welfare. She died of diphtheria in 1878; her daughters included Alix, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandra-feodorovna-alix-of-hesse">Empress Alexandra of Russia</a>, and Elisabeth, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchess-elizabeth-feodorovna">Grand Duchess Elizabeth Feodorovna</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/princess-alice-of-the-united-kingdom.jpg" alt="Princess Alice of the United Kingdom" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Backofen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alice,_Princess_Louis_of_Hesse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
